Article 23

1. Empowerment of women victims of violence shall be carried out in an integrated manner in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
2. Empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be directed to obtain opportunities and rights as human beings to be able to play a role and participate in activities:a. health;
b. education;

c. economy;
d. law;
e. employment;
f. politics and government.

